; Radio Mobile-style DBM Signal Level Color Definition (splat-classic.dcf)
; 10 discrete bands, strongest first. No interpolation in the engine.
; Format: dBm: red, green, blue
 -60: 200,  50,  50
 -64: 180, 160,  50
 -69: 150, 220,  50
 -73:  50, 220,  50
 -78:  30, 150,  30
 -82:  30, 200, 150
 -87:  50, 150, 220
 -91:  30,  80, 200
 -96:  20,  20, 150
-100:   0,   0, 100
; Navy floor: extend the weakest band to the noise floor so signal below
; -100 dBm stays navy instead of falling through to transparent black.
-200:   0,   0, 100
